# Agent scratch. The subagent-driven-development skill expects its
# workspace to be ignored — it never was here, and twice in one session
# a `git add -A` swept its reports and an in-flight regenerated tree
# into unrelated commits.
.superpowers/

# The copy-review gate's string index and result, written at the repo
# root by the skill that serves them.
copy-review/

# `make` builds the rastrillo binary here for the gate to exercise —
# scaffold-smoke.sh runs it against a throwaway app. Disposable output.
.build/

# `go generate ./...` renders the design-system gallery here so it can be
# looked at locally. The gallery is not committed — the website builds it
# with cmd/dsgen at a pinned version — and this copy is disposable.
.design-system/

# The gallery used to be committed here: 369 files, 20 MB, rewritten
# whole on every change to ui. It is not any more, and this line is what
# stops a `dsgen -out docs/design-system` from putting it back by habit.
docs/design-system/

# .claude/ is one machine's harness configuration — settings, hooks,
# worktrees, whatever that operator happens to run — and none of it is
# the project's. The one exception is the amadan house rules, which
# AGENTS.md sends every agent to read, so they have to arrive with a
# clone rather than with the person who last ran the installer. Until
# this repo held a tracked file under .claude/ nothing here mattered;
# now that it does, a `git add -A` would sweep the rest in.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/amadan/
